{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["כי תועבה — it is an object of loathing and contempt for the Egyptians to eat with the men of beyond the River, for they were despicable in their eyes and the men of Egypt were haughty, as written: קראתי לזאת [רהב] הם שבת. And similarly: ״כי תועבת מצרים כל רועה צאן״ — shepherds were held in contempt in their eyes, because sheep were abhorrent to them, as written: ״הן נזבח את תועבת מצרים לעיניהם ולא יסקלונו״ — a thing loathsome and abhorrent to the Egyptians, were we to slaughter it before them, they would not despise us enough to stone us — in the manner of disgrace, as we find with Shimei son of Gera: ״יצא יצוא [ומקלל]״ — ״ויסקל״ — he cursed David and stoned him with dirt in the manner of disgrace."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {0 "The bracketed [רהב] appears to be a scribal or editorial insertion; the citation does not match any known verse and its reference is uncertain. The phrase 'לצורינו' is rendered hyper-literally 'were we to slaughter it before them'; the reading is textually difficult."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:12.087405122Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}